-Subject: [PATCH] Pre-freeze corrections: dev startup split, honest
- verification message, atomic trade settlement
-
-- vite.config.js / package.json: split dev workflow into Vite frontend
-  (port 5173, proxying /api) and Express backend (port 3000, started
-  separately via npm start / npm run dev:server), matching the documented
-  clean dev configuration. Removed the embedded Express-in-Vite dev plugin.
-- server/config/config.js: load .env via dotenv in all entry points (this
-  was previously only done inside the removed Vite plugin, so .env loading
-  was silently broken for npm start / node server/server.js).
-- server/test/systemVerification.js: replaced the overclaiming
-  'ALL R01 - R10 REQUIREMENTS VERIFIED!' message with an accurate summary
-  that does not claim R08/R09 were established by the functional script.
-- server/services/database/ManagementOfDatabase.js: added
-  executeTradeSettlement() which wraps trade creation, both instruction
-  updates, and both account settlements in a single Mongoose session
-  transaction (R06/R11 concurrency review), falling back to sequential
-  writes with a one-time warning on standalone (non-replica-set) MongoDB
-  deployments that don't support transactions.
-- server/services/dealing/ManagementOfDealing.js: matching engine now uses
-  executeTradeSettlement() instead of separate unguarded writes per trade.
-- README.md: updated Quick Start, R06/R08/R09 status descriptions, and
-  added a section documenting the trade-settlement transaction behavior,
-  so the documentation matches the actual code.
-
-No R01-R10 functional behavior was changed; MongoDB remains the only
-persistent store. Automated functional verification, R08/R09 evaluation,
-concurrency load testing, and baseline freeze are still to be performed
-by the student.
